WEBVTT

NOTE
The narration of the Field walkthrough film (field-walkthrough.mp4), as
captions. They sit at the top of the picture (line:5%), so they never
cover the film's own caption bar at its foot. The words, with the times
they are spoken, are the narration script.

00:00:00.457 --> 00:00:03.334 line:5%
Chernozem Field, on a farm in Ukraine.

00:00:03.634 --> 00:00:07.744 line:5%
The overview shows the latest pass,
what needs doing, and your fields.

00:00:08.044 --> 00:00:12.540 line:5%
Every clear Sentinel-2 pass is read,
and the latest date is at the top.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.250 line:5%
Press a tile to pick out those fields
in the list on the right.

00:00:17.822 --> 00:00:20.453 line:5%
The farm's weather, and whether rain is coming.

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:25.233 line:5%
Fields shows every field on the satellite map,
tinted by its condition.

00:00:25.283 --> 00:00:28.343 line:5%
Pick one, or step through them with the arrows.

00:00:31.548 --> 00:00:35.506 line:5%
Its water, plant health,
stress and harvest readiness.

00:00:35.756 --> 00:00:38.389 line:5%
This season's plant health against normal years.

00:00:38.689 --> 00:00:43.879 line:5%
Data shows the field's record since 2019,
against the farm and normal years.

00:00:43.929 --> 00:00:46.839 line:5%
The red line marks the full-scale invasion.

00:00:47.139 --> 00:00:50.969 line:5%
Hover, or use the arrow keys,
to read any month's numbers.

00:00:51.481 --> 00:00:54.079 line:5%
Switch between plant health and water.

00:00:54.379 --> 00:00:58.739 line:5%
Download the outlines,
passes and history, or the season report.

00:00:59.353 --> 00:01:02.253 line:5%
Back on the overview, tell us what happened:

00:01:02.303 --> 00:01:07.793 line:5%
choose what it was and which field,
write what you saw and when, and add a photo.

00:01:12.965 --> 00:01:17.605 line:5%
Press Send. Your words stay
on screen while the report is saved.

00:01:18.253 --> 00:01:21.702 line:5%
The report opens the assistant,
with the field and the photo.

00:01:22.002 --> 00:01:24.953 line:5%
It stays with the chat,
beside the farm's readings.

00:01:25.253 --> 00:01:30.313 line:5%
The assistant answers from the farm's own
readings, its history, and the weather.

00:01:32.315 --> 00:01:37.635 line:5%
Here is a saved conversation:
how a field did this season, and what to watch.

00:01:38.385 --> 00:01:43.315 line:5%
Settings holds the farm's name and place,
its fields, and their crops.

00:01:47.074 --> 00:01:52.134 line:5%
Set a crop by picking what you sowed.
Until then, the detected crop is used.

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:58.124 line:5%
To add a field, press Add a field,
then click its corners on the satellite map.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.510 line:5%
The new field is saved, and analysed at once.

00:02:06.802 --> 00:02:11.942 line:5%
To remove a field, press its bin and confirm.
Its readings go with it.

00:02:13.616 --> 00:02:18.030 line:5%
Choose hectares, acres or mu,
and the whole app uses them.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.880 line:5%
Change farm is how you find your land:

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:24.780 line:5%
search for a village, paste coordinates,
or draw it on the map.

00:02:31.505 --> 00:02:35.765 line:5%
The map flies there,
and the fields around the pin are found.

00:02:36.657 --> 00:02:40.877 line:5%
Pick the fields that are yours,
or select them all, then save.

00:02:44.134 --> 00:02:46.924 line:5%
Come back after each satellite pass.

00:02:47.102 --> 00:02:50.460 line:5%
Register at chernozem.app
and read your own fields.
